#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# set_accuracy

#% text
# `set_accuracy(x, a)` gives the number `x` with its precision set so that its accuracy is `a` digits after the decimal point.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The precision is `a` plus the decimal logarithm of `abs(x)`, rounded up to a whole number of digits.

#% item
# It maps over lists.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
set_accuracy(1/3, 10)
#% output
#= 0.333333333

#% cell
set_accuracy(123456789/7, 4)
#% output
#= 17636684.143

#% cell
set_accuracy(2.5, 3)
#% output
#= 2.500

#% cell
accuracy(set_accuracy(1/3, 10))
#% output
#= 10.66098858484764

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `set_precision`, `accuracy`, `precision`
